ay!\nThe Sand Coreare located 3 \'infles north\nof Karab on the right side of the highway.\nThes and cover son enly med\nand can be seen from HWY 69. The hika\nitself short balfe round trip.\nThese and caves were man mac\nwhen they began ingthenin\nthe area. The mining process was short\nBed and we now have the spectacular\ncave templars. While exploring thum\ncoves, you will soos much graft, pleas\ndo not add to or defe there any fulher.\nyou have a ta sporn, malinaw north\non HWY 69 to Hogul Care and check\neut direstur tradka, luge rook collections,\nmale merican arch and shopping.\nPARKING\nMOQUI CAVE\nSAND CAVES\nCARPET\nKANAB\nDEARE\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nTR\nSAND CAVE\nPARKING\nSAPP\nKANAB\nMEILLY SPRILE\nPark\nST\n(baget\n(zimme','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Sand Caves\",\n  \"distance\": \"5.4 miles\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5577 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": null,\n  \"longitude\": null,\n  \"accessibility\": \"2WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"1-2 hrs\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Car\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 5.4 miles North on HWY 69. Just past mile post 69, turn right on the Best Friends Road. The parking area is immediately on your left. Park and look for a well beaten path going north.\",\n  \"description\": \"The Sand Caves are located 3 miles north of Kanab on the right side of the highway. These sand caves were man-made when they began mining the area. The mining process was short-lived, and now we have the spectacular cave formations. While exploring these caves, please do not add to or deface them any further.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>The Sand Caves are located 3 miles north of Kanab on the right side of the highway. These sand caves were man-made when they began mining the area. The mining process was short-lived, and now we have the spectacular cave formations. While exploring these caves, please do not add to or deface them any further.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"If you have more time, check out Moqui Cave just north on HWY 89. There are also dinosaur tracks, large rock collections, Native American arches, and shopping in Kanab.\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:48:47','2023-09-22 02:52:24'),(3,'trails',258,'',NULL,'L\nMARBLE CANYON LOOP\nSEMENT\nwww.\nPEPES\nLETTER\nLODGE\nN\nWAVE LOTTERY 1\nKanab Center\nKANAB\n(rear entrance)\n180 E 100 N\nPrecisely 8:30am the day before your hike.\nLeFEVRE OVERLOOK 2\nHere you have the rare chance to catch.\na glimpse of all the steps of the Crand\nStaircase.\nLeFevre Overlook\n-112 15.272, 36 49 805\n25.4 Miles from Kanab\nJACOB LAKE INN (COOKIES) 3\nMake sure you stop by Jacob Lake Inn\nand pick up some of their famous\nhomemade cookies. Locals say it\'s\nworth the drive just for the cookies!\nVERMILION CLIFFS OVERLOOK 4\nVermilion Cliffs is the 2nd step of\nthe five steps in the Grand Staircase,\non the Colorado Plateau in Northern\nArizona and Southern Utah.\nCONDOR VIEWING SITE 5\nA number of condors roost on top\nof the Vermilion Cliffs. This site offers\nvisitors a chance to see these enormous\nendangered birds in the wild.\nCLIFF DWELLERS LODGE 6\nOriginally a 1920\'s trading post, now\na stone and timber lodge and restaurant.\nThere are unique ruins of homes that are\nbuilt in the overhangs of fallen rocks.\nMARBLE CANYON 7\nRestaurant, bar and shopping. 9 min.\nwalk to Navajo Bridge. This rustic Old\nWest style Lodge is 5 min. from Lee\'s\nFerry and Lonely Dell Ranch.\nMARBLE CANYON LOOP\nKanab Utah\n-112 31.605, 37 2.877\nFREDONIA\nVISITOR SENTER\nThe scenic 190-mile Marble Canyon Loop traverses lonely Highway 89A in Utah and Arizona through the vast landscape of sandstone\ncliffs, sagebrush desert and ridges of pire and junipers. This is the perfect sightseeing opportunity during the seven months of the year\nthat the North Rim of the Grand Canyon is closed. There is so much to see and not enough hours in the day. Choose what you want to\nsee and plan another day to see the rest. he route begins in Kanab and heads south on hwy 89A and returns to Kanob for dinner and a\ngood night\'s rest. The Old West Town of Kanab has become a popular basecamp from which to discover the regions natural wonders.\nStart planning your adventure today at: www.VisitSouthernUtah.com\nKanab Visitor\'s Center 78 $ 100 E PHONE: 435.644.5033\nO\nWave Lottery\n180 E 100 N\nJacob Lake\n-112 13., 36 42.83\n36.6 Miles from Kanab\nPara Townsite\n-111 57 302, 37 15.060\n40 Miles from Kanab\n894\nADVENTURE MAP\nO\nGrand Canyon North Rim\n-112 3.126. 36 11.919\n83.16 Miles from Kanab\nt\nCondor Viewing Site\n-112 3.901, 36 40.258\n55.1 Miles from Kanal\nMes\n14\nM\nLee\'s Ferry\n111 35.222, 36 51.37\n83.4 Miles from Kanab\nMarble Canyon Lodge\n-111 33.251, 36 48.000\n77.4 Miles from Kanab\nCliff Dwellers Lodge\n111 46.193, 36 44.627\n69.2 Miles from Kanab\nVermilion Cliffs Overlook\n-1123.611, 36 43.366\n51.15 Miles from Kanab\nNAVAJO BRIDGE 8\nThe historical bridge is for pedestrians. The\nsecond, modern bridge is for cars to cross\nthe Colorado River. Beautiful place to walk\naround and do a little shopping.\nBitter Springs Jnct.\n91.1 Miles from Kanabi\n97.8 From Kanab via Page Az.\ntread lightly!\nLEE\'S FERRY\nThe only place within Clen Canyon,\nthat visitors can drive to the Colorado River.\nOver 700 miles of canyon country, right up\nto the first rapid in the Grand Canyon,\nHORSESHOE BEND 10\nOne of the most photographed areas\nof the Colorado River. One mile easy hike\nto the horseshoe shaped bend overlook\nof the Colorado River 1100 feet below.\nANTELOPE CANYON 11\nFamous and extremely beautiful slot\ncanyon on the Navajo Indian Reservation\nnear Page. It\'s the most visited slot canyon.\nMake reservations in advance.\nLAKE POWELL/GLEN CANYON DAM\nTour the spectacular dam that formed 12\nLake Powell. Back on Hwy 89 enjoy the\nviews of Lake Powell, or drive to the lake\nat Lone Rock.\nTOADSTOOL 13\nThis is the perfect family-friendly hike.\nIt is 1 mile to the Toadstools. You will\nget the feeling of being on another\nplane. It is especially beautiful at\nsunsel.\nPARIA 14\nDescend into a valley with the remains\nof the Paria Ghost Town and cemetery\nsite. Surrounded by amazingly colorful\nrocks and multi colored layered cliffs.\ni\nA111 524,37 6.066\nToadstoo\nMAT\n44.67 Miles from Kana\nLIFE\nUTAH\nELEVATED\n12\n10\nTORS\nO Lake Powell\n-111 32.632, 37 1.218\n64.5 Miles from Kanab\nW\nXUT)\nSAPP\nD\nAnte ope Canyon\n111 24.511, 34 53.847\n78.5 Miles from Kenab\nNavajo Caryon Bridg\n111. 37.009, 36 49.035\n77.65 Miles from Kanab\nHorseslive Band\n11 30.171, 36 52.597\n76.6 Wiles from Kanab\nKANAB\nHOLLY DESPOKE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Marble Canyon Loop\",\n  \"distance\": \"190 miles\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Seven months of the year\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"-112 31.605, 37 2.877\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.048\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.527\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Accessible\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"N/A\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Car\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"Starts in Kanab, Utah and follows Highway 89A\",\n  \"description\": \"The scenic 190-mile Marble Canyon Loop traverses lonely Highway 89A in Utah and Arizona through the vast landscape of sandstone cliffs, sagebrush desert, and ridges of pine and junipers. This is the perfect sightseeing opportunity during the seven months of the year that the North Rim of the Grand Canyon is closed.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>The scenic 190-mile Marble Canyon Loop traverses lonely Highway 89A in Utah and Arizona through the vast landscape of sandstone cliffs, sagebrush desert, and ridges of pine and junipers. This is the perfect sightseeing opportunity during the seven months of the year that the North Rim of the Grand Canyon is closed.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"The Old West Town of Kanab has become a popular basecamp from which to discover the region\'s natural wonders. Start planning your adventure today at: www.VisitSouthernUtah.com\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:48:52','2023-09-22 02:52:36'),(4,'trails',259,'',NULL,'INCHWORM\nARCH\nINCHWORM\nARCH\nSANT\n#DE\nSAL\n9.1 mi\nA\nNEPHI\nCANYON\nKANAB 9.5 mi\nADVENTURE MAP\nA810\nPASTURE\nYou\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nELEVATION:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nHALF DAY\nDIFFICULTY: EASY RIDE/ VERY SANDY\n.25 MILES ROUND TRIP\nYEAR ROUND\nATV OR 4WD\nGETTING THERE:\n• From Kanab drive East on HWY 89, and turn left at Johnson Canyon (just past milepost 551.\nTravel 9.1 miles to the Nephi Postures Troilhood on your right, Unload your ATV hoc.\nTake road #556 for about 8 miles.\nSTAPLE AXUM ARWO\nROAD\nYES\n•The road will drep into a vallay, then turn right at road #558.\n• Drive 1 mile, TAKE THE FIRST LEFT. (If you reach the corral you\'ve gone to fort.\n• Confinue 1.5 miles, when the road forks stay left.\nThe mood will and. There you will see a brown \"No Vahi-les\" sigr-pork hem\n.\nHiking down the sand hill behind the No Vehicle, sign.\n• You will mearder southeast for about 50 yards, and then head back west to a rock ledge\noverlock, where you can view the double arch.\n5854 FEET\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 S 100 E\nSWATHEDAY\nDISCLAIMER:\n*This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassaole when wer. Please respect\nPrivate Properly. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water,\nfood, aunscreen, and supplies, Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacs or deface the frock ort. Leave no trace of your visit so\nothers may enjoy.\nPHONE 435.644.5033\n556\n204\nERFACE\nFIRST LEFT\n8 mi\nWhile out on a backpacking trip, a\ngroup of Kando Boy Scouts ciscovered.\nand named this arch \"Inchwarm Arch\".\nIt\'s been a local favorite for generations.\nSean from just the right angle, this\ndouble arch resembles a long\ninchworn slowly crawling its way down\nclong the rocks. You have to position\nyourself just right by hiking down the\ncanyon and looking up. A 4WD or\nATV is required to get to the arch be\ncause of the deep sand. This is a fun\nand relaxing ride. There are amazing\nvews of the White Cliffs.\nROAD\nENDS CORRAL A\n1.5 mi\nINCHWORM\nARCH\nGPS 37, 10037\n112,33401\nC\n1 mi\n558\nSAND HEL\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nt\nWASTRAY\nUT\nKANAB\nMARICALLY UNSPOILED\nN\n558\n554\n556\nKANAB\nMe EmpLCO','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Inchworm Arch\",\n  \"distance\": \"0.25 miles round trip\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5854 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.10037\",\n  \"longitude\": \"112.33401\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"ATV or 4WD required\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Half day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"ATV or 4WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab drive East on HWY 89, and turn left at Johnson Canyon (just past milepost 55). Travel 9.1 miles to the Nephi Posture Trailhead on your right. Unload your ATV here. Take road #556 for about 8 miles. The road will drop into a valley, then turn right at road #558. Drive 1 mile, take the first left, and continue 1.5 miles. When the road forks, stay left. The road will end and you will see a brown \\\"No Vehicles\\\" sign. Hike down the sand hill behind the sign.\",\n  \"description\": \"While out on a backpacking trip, a group of Kando Boy Scouts discovered and named this arch \\\"Inchworm Arch\\\". It\'s been a local favorite for generations. Seen from just the right angle, this double arch resembles a long inchworm slowly crawling its way along the rocks. You have to position yourself just right by hiking down the canyon and looking up. A 4WD or ATV is required to get to the arch because of the deep sand. This is a fun and relaxing ride. There are amazing views of the White Cliffs.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>While out on a backpacking trip, a group of Kando Boy Scouts discovered and named this arch \\\"Inchworm Arch\\\". It\'s been a local favorite for generations. Seen from just the right angle, this double arch resembles a long inchworm slowly crawling its way along the rocks. You have to position yourself just right by hiking down the canyon and looking up. A 4WD or ATV is required to get to the arch because of the deep sand. This is a fun and relaxing ride. There are amazing views of the White Cliffs.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"DISCLAIMER: *This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy. Phone: 435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:48:58','2023-09-22 02:52:57'),(5,'trails',135,'',NULL,'WIRE PASS/BUCKSKIN GULCH\nSLOT CANYON\nSTRA\nKANAB 38.6 mi\n89 N\nO\nDOUBLEARCH -0.0\nCOYOTE BUTTES\n4 OPENING\nBOULDER\n5 CHOKE\nMIRE PASS TH\n3 JO\nWIFE\n2 PASS\nSLOT\n6\n5 MILE\nMARK\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nADVENTURE MAP\n80 10 1\nBEST SEASON:\nPERMIT:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nWIRE PASS/BUCKSKIN GULCH\nSLOT CANYON\nELEVATION:\nGETTING THERE:\nSPRING SUMNER FALL\n8.4 mi\nWIRE PASS\nTRAILHEAD\nYES\n21 MILES ONE WAY\n• From Konab, drive 38,6 miles Cust on IIWY 39.\n• Just past mile post 26, turn right on to the House Rock Valley Road.\nTravel B.4 miles to the Wire Pass Trailhead parking lot located on the right.\nCross the road and hike the wash downstream about 1.5 mile where the canyon begins to narrow.\nYou will pass through 3 sections of slots on your way to the confluence with Buckskin Gulch.\nNOTE\n12 HRS - 2 DAYS\nDIFFICULT\nBe sure you are aware of weather conditions and flashflood potential before entering the canyon. No\ndrinking water is available in Buckskin Gulch, so carry plenty of water. You may encounter several\nabstacles such as miles of streambed rocks, muddy areas, deep and stagnant water pools, foller rocks\nor log jams. It is suggested to bring 40 t. of rope for lowering packs and for hand line use.\nDISCLAIMER:\nWYROLF\nYES\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPusars\n4860 FEET\nBUCKSKIN GULCH\nTRAILHEAD\n11.5 mi\nBuckskin Gulch is one of the longest alor\nconyors in the world, I passes through 16\nmiles of amazing rock formations and smooth y\nrising and falling form of sandstone walls.\nfrom the Wire Pess railhead, the first few\nmiles follow an open wash. At Roughly\na mile visitors can observe\npetroglyphs. At 15 miles you will reach the\ncanfluence with Buckskin Gulch, sandstone\nwalls will appear on both sides of the\nwash as it enters the narrows. Although the\nhikes fairly tame at the beginning, as you\ntravel deeper into the canyon, you will begin.\nto encounter obstacles inclucing giant boulder\njams and at times deep pools of water that con\nlinger for months after a flood. Hiking this\nbeautiful canyon should only be crempted by\nvery experienced and well prepared hikers.\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\nHIGHWAY 89\nIM\nCLARE\nKANAB\nUT\nAPP\nMEGALLY INSPIL.CO','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch\",\n  \"distance\": \"8.4 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Spring, Summer, Fall\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Difficult\",\n  \"elevation\": \"4860 FEET\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.0899\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.1466\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Yes\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"12 HRS - 2 DAYS\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"4x4 recommended\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 38.6 miles east on Hwy 89. Just past mile post 26, turn right onto the House Rock Valley Road. Travel 4 miles to the Wire Pass Trailhead parking lot located on the right. Cross the road and hike the wash downstream about 1.5 miles where the canyon begins to narrow. You will pass through 3 sections of slots on your way to the confluence with Buckskin Gulch.\",\n  \"description\": \"Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch is a slot canyon trail located near Kanab. It offers a challenging and adventurous hiking experience. The trail starts at Wire Pass Trailhead and goes through a wash before entering the narrow sections of the canyon. Hiking deeper into the canyon, hikers will encounter obstacles such as giant boulder jams and deep pools of water. The canyon is known for its stunning rock formations and sandstone walls.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Wire Pass/Buckskin Gulch is a slot canyon trail located near Kanab. It offers a challenging and adventurous hiking experience. The trail starts at Wire Pass Trailhead and goes through a wash before entering the narrow sections of the canyon. Hiking deeper into the canyon, hikers will encounter obstacles such as giant boulder jams and deep pools of water. The canyon is known for its stunning rock formations and sandstone walls.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Be sure to check weather conditions and flash flood potential before entering the canyon. Carry plenty of water as there is no drinking water available in Buckskin Gulch. It is recommended to bring rope for lowering packs and for hand line use. Respect private property and leave no trace of your visit.\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:49:04','2023-09-22 02:53:17'),(6,'trails',261,'',NULL,'ALSTROM POINT\n4WD\n4WD\nFEATLOHNING SEEINENTAL\n56 mi\nKANAB\nETHAN\nBIG\nWATER\nVISITOR\nCENTER\nALLEN K8000/300\nLOST\n(89)\nADVENTURE MAP\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nALSTROM POINT\nPAGE\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nYES\nYEAR ROUND\nMODERATE-DIFFICULT\n330\n4WD\n14 mi\nNO\nFULL DAY\nK8150\nGETTING THERE\n• From Kenab, drive 56 miles East on HWY 89.\n• Just past mile post 7. tum left on the Ethan Allen Road.\n4600 FEET\n• Drive approximately 0.3 miles and turn right on K8000/300.\n• Follow this good gravel road for 14 miles.\nTurn right on K8200/340 and drive 4.23 miles\n• Turn right on K8180 for 6.88 miles to Alstrom Point.\n• This road travels over slick rock and can be hard to follow. There are a few rock cairns on the trail.\nNOTE.\nA few sections require a high clearance 4 wheal crive vehicle. This is very remoto desert, with limited\nto NO cell phone service. Be prepared, have a vehicle in good working order and bring plenty of food,\nwater, gas and a shovel\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen,\nand supplies. Cell phore service is non-existent ir most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so others may enjoy.\"\nKane County Office of Tourism: 78 S 100 E PHONE: 435.644.5033\nPHONE: 435.644.5033 www.VisitSouthernUtah.com\nThis off road adventure takes you to\nAlstrom Point, one of the best overlooks\non Leke Powell. A photographers dream,\nthe breathtaking views are heightened cr\nsunrise and sunset. You can see Navaja\nMountain in the distance, sacred\nground to the native american people\nand their traditions. This is one of the\nmost scenic and remote areas in the Glen\nCanyon Recreation Area. This drive is not\nrecommended at right or if the road is\nwet. The clay road goes up and down\nin the middle of huge coryons. You will\nalso enjoy the badlands along the way.\nThere are plenty of camping sites if you\nchoose to spend the night.\n300\nK8200\n4.23 mi\nCROSBY CANYON\nOVERLOOK\nLAKE\nPOWELL\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nMODE\n6.88 mi\nK8180\nTOVE\nAFP\nN\nALSTROM\nPOINT\nTERMAR\nGPS 37 3.538\n111 21 855\nKANAB\nMac. EPILE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Alstrom Point\",\n  \"distance\": \"56 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year-round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate-difficult\",\n  \"elevation\": \"330 ft\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.059\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-111.364\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"4WD vehicle\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": false,\n  \"reservation_required\": false,\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Full day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"K8150\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 56 miles East on HWY 89. Just past mile post 7, turn left on the Ethan Allen Road. Drive approximately 0.3 miles and turn right on K8000/300. Follow this good gravel road for 14 miles. Turn right on K8200/340 and drive 4.23 miles. Turn right on K8180 for 6.88 miles to Alstrom Point. This road travels over slick rock and can be hard to follow. There are a few rock cairns on the trail.\",\n  \"description\": \"This off-road adventure takes you to Alstrom Point, one of the best overlooks on Lake Powell. A photographer\'s dream, the breathtaking views are heightened during sunrise and sunset. You can see Navajo Mountain in the distance, sacred ground to the Native American people and their traditions. This is one of the most scenic and remote areas in the Glen Canyon Recreation Area. This drive is not recommended at night or if the road is wet. The clay road goes up and down in the middle of huge canyons. You will also enjoy the badlands along the way. There are plenty of camping sites if you choose to spend the night.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"This off-road adventure takes you to Alstrom Point, one of the best overlooks on Lake Powell. A photographer\'s dream, the breathtaking views are heightened during sunrise and sunset. You can see Navajo Mountain in the distance, sacred ground to the Native American people and their traditions. This is one of the most scenic and remote areas in the Glen Canyon Recreation Area. This drive is not recommended at night or if the road is wet. The clay road goes up and down in the middle of huge canyons. You will also enjoy the badlands along the way. There are plenty of camping sites if you choose to spend the night.\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Please note that a few sections require a high clearance 4-wheel drive vehicle. This is a very remote desert with limited to no cell phone service. Be prepared by having a vehicle in good working order and bring plenty of food, water, gas, and a shovel. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may become impassable when wet. Please respect private property and do not remove artifacts or deface rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:49:12','2023-09-22 02:53:39'),(7,'trails',262,'',NULL,'BELLY OF THE DRAGON\nEXPLORE\nHollow\nS\nGPS 37 11.639\n112 39.658\n* 56087\nRear Co\nENTRANCE BELLY OF\nTHE DRAGON\nSHORT HIKE\nGraja.\n(9)\nMILE\n0\nBELLY OF THE DRAGON\nEXPLORE/HIKE\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\n.5 mi\nENTRANCE\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY\nELEVATION:\nMOUNT\nCARMEL\nJUNCTION\n(5496\n14.2 mi\nCHILD\n5484\nNO\nYEAR ROUND\n2WD\nSHORT DISTANCE\nGETTING THERE\n* From Kanab, dr ve about 16 miles north on HWY 89.\n• After past mile pos 80, ccross from the Zion National Park sign turn left onto the dirt road.\n• Contintinue on the dirt road for a short cistance veer left.\n• Park at the top of the hill.\n• Walk up the hill and you will see the opening to the tunnel.\n• F you are going in the late afternoon you may want a flash light.\n• If you are feeling adverterous you may continue hiking up the wash.\nis 5 miles to the small slot canyon.\n* You can turn around cnylime and go back the same way you come, in the wash.\n1-2 HOURS\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nEASY\n6000 FEET\nJarn\nThe Belly of the Dragon is quite the\nadventerous, scenic, lime hike. This\ncarved tunnel hike passes under highway\n89, and is used as a drainage for the upper\ncanyons that feeds into North Fark River.\nDO NOT enter the tunnel under any\nrainy conditions. There are few sco\nof rock scrambling to get up and through.\nthe tunnel There are carvings in the rock\nat the entrance to the tunnel. Please respect\nThese walls and adc no more we wish to\nkeep the natural beauty of this orac\nThrough the tunnel is a short hike,\nyou may continue up the wash for about 4\nmiles, it ancs of a beautiful Intle slot canyon\nThere is amazing scenery around every\nbend. We are excited to have you come\nand explore our backyard with us.\n3.4 mi\nSLOT\nCANYON\nBELLY OF\nTHE DRAGON\nLONGER HIKE\n1192320\nADVENTURE MAP tread lightly!\n88 O\nNORTH\n(89\nKANAB\nMARICALLY UNSPOILE\nWash\nKANAB\nLIFE\nWANTVAN\nИТАН UT KANAB\nELEVATED\nCAPP\nMILLE','{\n   \"trail_name\": \"Belly of the Dragon\",\n   \"distance\": \"0.5 mi\",\n   \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n   \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n   \"elevation\": \"6000 feet\",\n   \"latitude\": \"37.193983\",\n   \"longitude\": \"-112.660967\",\n   \"accessibility\": \"2WD\",\n   \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n   \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n   \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"1-2 hours\",\n   \"vehicle\": \"Car\",\n   \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive about 16 miles north on HWY 89. After passing mile post 80, cross from the Zion National Park sign and turn left onto the dirt road. Continue on the dirt road for a short distance and veer left. Park at the top of the hill. Walk up the hill and you will see the opening to the tunnel.\",\n   \"description\": \"The Belly of the Dragon is quite an adventurous and scenic hike. This carved tunnel hike passes under highway 89 and is used as a drainage for the upper canyons that feeds into North Fork River. Do not enter the tunnel under any rainy conditions. There are few sections of rock scrambling to get up and through the tunnel. There are carvings in the rock at the entrance to the tunnel. Please respect these walls and do not deface them. Through the tunnel is a short hike, and you may continue up the wash for about 4 miles to reach a beautiful narrow slot canyon with amazing scenery around every bend. We are excited to have you come and explore our backyard with us.\",\n   \"description_html\": \"<p>The Belly of the Dragon is quite an adventurous and scenic hike. This carved tunnel hike passes under highway 89 and is used as a drainage for the upper canyons that feeds into North Fork River. Do not enter the tunnel under any rainy conditions. There are few sections of rock scrambling to get up and through the tunnel. There are carvings in the rock at the entrance to the tunnel. Please respect these walls and do not deface them. Through the tunnel is a short hike, and you may continue up the wash for about 4 miles to reach a beautiful narrow slot canyon with amazing scenery around every bend. We are excited to have you come and explore our backyard with us.</p>\",\n   \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\",\n}','2023-09-22 02:49:23','2023-09-22 02:54:01'),(8,'trails',263,'',NULL,'ASPEN MIRROR\nLAKE\nMouse\nBONN\nPLEASE KEEP THIS\nSPECIAL PLACE\nPRISTINE\nPACK IT IN-PACK IT OUT\nNavajo Lake\nNAVAJO\nLAKE\nCAMPGROUND\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nADVENTURE MAP\nSo 60 KA\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nASPEN MIRROR\nLAKE\nGETTING THERE:\nGPS 37.517\n112.682\nASPEN MIRROR LAKE\nNO\nYEAR ROUND\nstrates t\n2WD\nEASY STROLL\n3 HOURS TO FULL DAY\nEASY\n• From Karab, drive 40 miles North or HWY 89.\n• Turn left onto HWY 14.\n• Drive approximately 11.1 miles and turn right on FR057\n• Drive a short distance and turn right on to the Markagunt Plateau OHV Trail.\n• Fork here.\n•\nBring a lunch and enjoy the trails.\n8500 FEET\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen,\nand supplies. Cell phore service is non-existentir most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so others may enjoy.\"\nKane County Visitor\'s Center: 78 $ 100 E PHONE: 435.644.5033 www.VisitSouthernUtah.com\nTucked away from the main road, his lake\nis surrounded by pires and aspen frees\nmaking it a spectacular destination in the fall,\nor to enjoy cooler temperatures in the summer\nmonths. The aspens ref ecting on the lake is a\nphotographers dream, so be sure to\nbring a camera. The loke is stocked\nwith rainbow trout that provides sone\namazing fishing opportunities You can enjoy\ntime watching the wildlife. The lake is home to\nmany kinds of wildlife; deer, chipmunks,\nsquirrels, faxes, frogs end snakes. There are\nmany trois in the area for hiking, biking, and\nOHV\'s. Visit Duck Creek Village for a bine to\neat. There is so much to do here check with\nthe Dixie National Forest Visitor Center for\nmore trails information 435 865-3730.\n11.1 mi\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\ncomforta\nNUMUNE\nANTRON\nKU\nSAPP\n(14)\n<<NORTH>\n89\nN\n40 mi-\nKANAB\nKANAB\nMaticALLY US','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Aspen Mirror Lake\",\n  \"distance\": 11.1,\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": 8500,\n  \"latitude\": 37.517,\n  \"longitude\": 112.682,\n  \"accessibility\": \"2WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": false,\n  \"reservation_required\": false,\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"3 hours to full day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"From Kanab, drive 40 miles North on HWY 89. Turn left onto HWY 14. Drive approximately 11.1 miles and turn right on FR057. Drive a short distance and turn right onto the Markagunt Plateau OHV Trail. Fork here.\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 40 miles North on HWY 89. Turn left onto HWY 14. Drive approximately 11.1 miles and turn right on FR057. Drive a short distance and turn right onto the Markagunt Plateau OHV Trail. Fork here.\",\n  \"description\": \"Tucked away from the main road, Aspen Mirror Lake is surrounded by pines and aspen trees, making it a spectacular destination in the fall or to enjoy cooler temperatures in the summer months. The aspens reflecting on the lake is a photographer\'s dream, so be sure to bring a camera. The lake is stocked with rainbow trout, providing some amazing fishing opportunities. You can also enjoy watching the wildlife, including deer, chipmunks, squirrels, foxes, frogs, and snakes. There are many trails in the area for hiking, biking, and OHVs. Visit Duck Creek Village for a bite to eat. For more trail information, check with the Dixie National Forest Visitor Center at 435-865-3730.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"Tucked away from the main road, <strong>Aspen Mirror Lake</strong> is surrounded by pines and aspen trees, making it a spectacular destination in the fall or to enjoy cooler temperatures in the summer months. The aspens reflecting on the lake is a photographer\'s dream, so be sure to bring a camera. The lake is stocked with rainbow trout, providing some amazing fishing opportunities. You can also enjoy watching the wildlife, including deer, chipmunks, squirrels, foxes, frogs, and snakes. There are many trails in the area for hiking, biking, and OHVs. Visit Duck Creek Village for a bite to eat. For more trail information, check with the Dixie National Forest Visitor Center at 435-865-3730.\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Disclaimer: This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may become impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art\'. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\\n\\nKane County Visitor\'s Center: 78 $ 100 E, Phone: 435.644.5033, Website: www.VisitSouthernUtah.com\"\n}','2023-09-22 02:49:40','2023-09-22 02:54:26'),(9,'trails',264,'',NULL,'BEST FRIENDS\nANIMAL SANCTUARY\nBest Friends, on cny given day is home to around 1,700 animals from: cats and dogs, horses and pigs, birds and\nrabbits. Here they receive love, medical care and most importantly, the opportunity to find families of their own.\nFor some, it\'s the first time they\'ve known kindness and companionship, for all it\'s a life saving second chance.\nNORTH\nENIHANCE\nTu Hyuny 89\nJUST A RE