 ravines and desert areas. It is a moderately difficult trail best enjoyed in the cooler seasons. Please note that cell phone service is limited in the area.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"The map and directions provided are intended for general guidance only. Always check road and weather conditions, as they can be unpredictable. Dirt roads may be impassable after rain. Please respect private property and leave no trace during your visit. Be prepared with extra water, food, sunscreen, and appropriate gear. Phone: 435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:30:35','2023-09-22 02:32:43'),(16,'trails',271,'',NULL,'BUNTING\nHIKE\n12 Tapet\nBUNTING\nHIKE\nNO\nXe\nCOTTONWOOD 23 mi\nCANYON\nTRAIL\nADVENTURE MAP\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nGETTING THERE\nBUNTING\nTRAIL\n2.3 mi\nAusting\n200\nYES\n1.6 MILES TO THE TOP\nHALF DAY\nYEAR ROUND\nHARD AND STEEP\n5040-5860 FEET\nFrom Muin Street, heud suuth on HWY 89A uppruxirately 1.2 miles\n• Turn right orto Konob Crook Drive.\n• Drive 2 miles and at the top of the hill, turn right onto Stanfield Drive.\n• The first parking area on the right is for the Bunting Trail.\nHead north to the trailhead.\n1 mi\nt6 mi\nDINOSAUR\nTRACKS\n2WD\nna mile take a short detour to see the dinosour tracks.\nWatch for the signs on your left handing up a wash.\n• The signs will lead you to the tracks on a big sandstone boulder.\n• Go back the way you come and start back on the trail to the too.\n• NOTE: If you hike the Spur Troil, please proceed with caution.\nThis is a self designated path with no dearly marked trail.\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo