that connects southern Utah and northern Arizona, passing through popular destinations such as Bryce Canyon National Park and Zion National Park. Along the way, there are various accommodations and attractions to explore.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": null\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:17','2023-09-22 02:34:50'),(23,'trails',278,'',NULL,'GREENHALCH\nHIKE/EQUESTRIAN\nGREENHALGH\nHIKE\n3600\nGREENHALGH\nTRAIL\nADVENTURE MAP\nATV\nBRIDGE\nHEAD NORTH\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKE\nAVERAGE TIME\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nGREENHALGH3\nKANAB\nGETTING THERE\n•From the center of town haad north on HWY 89,\nAfter mile post 66 turn left onto the dirt mac\n• When the road forks stay left.\nHOG\nCANYON\nYEAR ROUND\n4 MILES ROUND TRIP\n3 HOURS\nNO\nFORU\n2WD\nMODERATE\n5850 FEET\n• At 5 miles the Greenholgh trailhead is on your right.\nEQUESTRIAN\n2 mil\n• At the next fork stay right.\n• Fark at the ATV bridge. Start your hike here.\n• Cross the ATV bridge one go left following the dirt road.\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nHEADX\nNORTH\nHERE\n• After mile post 65 turn left on the dirt road. Park Fere.\n• The trail will be on the west and will head north.\nDISCLAIMER\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nATV\nBRIDGE\n=1\nThis trail is named for the Greenhalgh brothers,\ntwo local characters who homostoaded the\n2.7 mi\nEQUESTRIAN\nPARKING\ngrea in 1900\'s. The two sons, Harry and\nWillard look the ranch over after their father\nded and continued the operation from the\n1940\'s into the 1960\'s, The Greenhaighs\nused this trail to run cattle above and\nwest of Trail Canyon. The boys are buried\nin the Kanas cemetary. The trail climbs to a\nsweeping vista al the too at the Vermilion\nCliffs in Trai Canyon. This trail is part of the\noriginal mail route between Kanab anc\nSpringdae, which was a several mile, difficull\nhorseback ride from Kannb to the Saunesburg\nClifis where the puigoing mail bag was\nlowered cown a cliff to the mailman. The rape\nwas pulled back up and the incoming bag\nelurred a Konab. Enjoy the tral\nΚΑΝΑΒ\nJARDIN\nHOG\nCANYON\nMILE\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\nNORTH\n89\n5754\nDIY\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\nCanyon\n3117\nUT KANAB\nAPP\nM.CO','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Greenhalgh\",\n  \"distance\": \"4 miles round trip\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Moderate\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5850 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.1088\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.5450\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"2WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"3 hours\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"2WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From the center of town head north on HWY 89. After mile post 66, turn left onto the dirt road. When the road forks, stay left. At 5 miles, the Greenhalgh trailhead is on your right. Park at the ATV bridge. Start your hike here. Cross the ATV bridge and go left, following the dirt road.\",\n  \"description\": \"This trail is named for the Greenhalgh brothers, two local characters who homesteaded the area in the 1900\'s. The two sons, Harry and Willard, took over the ranch after their father died and continued the operation from the 1940\'s into the 1960\'s. The Greenhalghs used this trail to run cattle above and west of Trail Canyon. The boys are buried in the Kanab cemetery. The trail climbs to a sweeping vista atop the Vermilion Cliffs in Trail Canyon. This trail is part of the original mail route between Kanab and Springdale, which was a several-mile, difficult horseback ride from Kanab to the Saunesburg Cliffs, where the outgoing mail bag was lowered down a cliff to the mailman. The rope was pulled back up and the incoming bag was returned to Kanab. Enjoy the trail and tread lightly!\",\n  \"description_html\": \"This trail is named for the Greenhalgh brothers, two local characters who homesteaded the area in the 1900\'s. The two sons, Harry and Willard, took over the ranch after their father died and continued the operation from the 1940\'s into the 1960\'s. The Greenhalghs used this trail to run cattle above and west of Trail Canyon. The boys are buried in the Kanab cemetery. The trail climbs to a sweeping vista atop the Vermilion Cliffs in Trail Canyon. This trail is part of the original mail route between Kanab and Springdale, which was a several-mile, difficult horseback ride from Kanab to the Saunesburg Cliffs, where the outgoing mail bag was lowered down a cliff to the mailman. The rope was pulled back up and the incoming bag was returned to Kanab. Enjoy the trail and tread lightly!\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\",\n  \"PHONE\": \"435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:23','2023-09-22 02:35:16'),(24,'trails',279,'',NULL,'HELL DIVE\nPICTOGRAPHS\nHELL DIVE\nPICTOGRAPHS\n******************\nCORAL PINK SAND DUNES\nJas\nAGILA\nMAIRA ETAME\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON\nHIKING\nVEHICLE: HIGH CLEARANCE 4WD/ATV\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nSPRING SUMMER\nAND FALL\n51\nVERY DIFFICULT IN SPOTS.\nSOME EXTREME ROCK CRAWLING.\nADVENTURE MAP RESPECT\nYES\n.25 MILE\nGETTING THERE:\n* Drive 8 miles north of Karab, just pust Milepost 71, um west ono Hancock Road.\n• Turn left on Road 50. 4WD is required from here.\nJANS\n3.44 mi\n* The next inte section, turn right on road 51.\n* When the road T\'s stay left to the end of the road.\n* Park, look eus ane you will see the alcove and a faint trail\n* Hike along the wall until you reach the clcove.\n5525 FEET\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use on y. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stey on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always oring extra water,\nfood, sunscreen, and supplies Cell phone service is nonexistent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifact or deface the \'rock art, Leave no trace of your visit so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 S 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\n1 DAY\nSAND\nSPRINGS Ant\nBIG\nSAND\nDUNE\nHANCOCK ROAD\n6.27 mi\nsteer\nLAKINTO\nEXTREME\nROCK CLIMBING\nNOT RECOMMENDED\n3.5 mi\n50\nLecals call this sile Medicine Man Cave\nbecause of the many intriguing rock ar\npictographs and ceremonial symbols.\nEarly farmers may have used this area\nfor food storage and preparation, as\nevidenced by the many metate grincing\nlocations, grooves and storage pits.\nThis cave may have been a place for\nwomen to have child birth, hence the\nbabies feet and the fertility God\nKokopelli pained on the walls.\nWhatever the cove\'s use, you feel of\ncadear\npeaceful spiritual renewal here.\nGelling to Hell Dive cun be somewhat\nchallenging high clearance 4 wheel\ndrive is required. Use road 51; 52\nrequires extreme rock climbing and\nshould be avoided. Be sure to step and\nenjoy the spectacular views of Zion in\nthe distance. Please do not touch or\ndeface rock art and leave no trace.\n2.26 mi\n51\nKANAB\nMagicELLY UNSPOILED\nINDIAN CANYON\nPICTOGRAPHS\nKANAB 8 mi\nN\nNAB TRAI\nUT\nAPP\nHELL DIVE\nPICTOGRAPHS\nGPS 37 2.650\n112 38.437\nO PROTECT KANAB ABRA KANABRA! UTAH\nLITH\nNEWLY INSPEILED\nwww.visitsouthernutah.com ERVATIO','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Hell Dive Pictographs\",\n  \"distance\": \"3.44 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Spring, Summer, and Fall\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Very Difficult\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5525 FEET\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.044167\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.640617\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"High Clearance 4WD/ATV Required\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": 4,\n  \"vehicle\": \"High Clearance 4WD/ATV\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"Drive 8 miles north of Kanab, just past Milepost 71, turn west onto Hancock Road. Turn left on Road 50. 4WD is required from here. At the next intersection, turn right on Road 51. When the road T\'s, stay left to the end of the road. Park and hike along the wall until you reach the alcove and the trail.\",\n  \"description\": \"Hell Dive is a challenging hike to view ancient rock art pictographs in an alcove. The trail is known for extreme rock crawling and requires a high clearance 4WD or ATV. The hike is very difficult in spots, but offers spectacular views of Zion in the distance. Please respect the rock art and leave no trace.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Hell Dive is a challenging hike to view ancient rock art pictographs in an alcove. The trail is known for extreme rock crawling and requires a high clearance 4WD or ATV. The hike is very difficult in spots, but offers spectacular views of Zion in the distance. Please respect the rock art and leave no trace.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is nonexistent in most areas. Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy. For more information, visit the Kanab Visitor\'s Center.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:29','2023-09-22 02:35:33'),(25,'trails',280,'',NULL,'KANAB HERITAGE\nWALKING TOUR\nThe City of Kanab is rich in heritage. Mony of the homes and buildings built in the early pioneer days of Kanab\'s history\nare still standing. The Heritage Walking Tour shown on these pages will allow you to step back for a moment to he\ndays of pioneer life. NOTE: The homes are NOT open to the public. Please respect the privacy of the residents.\nKane County Visitor Center: 78 S 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\n1. THE HERITAGE HOUSE\nOn the corner of Main and 100 Saub, his\nhouse was built for Henry Bowman in 1894\nand has since been restored to its original\nThe Heritage is on the\nNational Register and is a monument to the\npast. Wilhir its walls is a collection of relics\nand souvenirs, not on y of the people who\nlived there, but of friends and neighbors also.\nThis home can be seen during the summer\nmonths. Visit the Kane County Visitors Center\nfor more information.\n4. JOHNSON/HICKS HOTEL AND\nRESTAURANT\nBuilt in 1984 as a residence, this ma estic\nhome was later used as a hotel and\nrestaurant by Mrs. Nellie McAllister and\nsubsequently purchased by Art Brown\nCurrently the home is Purple Sage Bed\nand Breakfast.\ntread lightly!\n7. IDS CHURCH AND FAMILY HISTORY\nVISITORS CENTER\nThe first Moman settlers to this area erected\nthis church. The building has undergone\nseveral rencvations and additions. Look for\nthe Moror Battalior historical marker, as\nwell as a marker commeruling the first\nall women city counci in the United States,\n11912-19141 The Church was remodeled\nin 2013 and now serves as the Family\nHistory Visitors Cente: Stop by and leam\nabout your family history.\nPANNONSER\n10. IFV STEWART & DILWORTH F\nWOOLLEY HOUSE\nThis home at 106 West 100 North was\nbuilt in 1889 by Levi Stewart, for his wife\nArtimacy. Stowart was sent to colonize at\nre and\nstrengthen the settlement of Kanub. After\nthe death of Levi, Artimasy sold the Foire to\nDilworth Wooley Jr. in 1889. Edwin\'s known\nfor bringing tourism to Southern Utah and\nthe Grand Canyon. In 1909 he brought the\nfirst automobile to Kanab. His daughter\nMary Wooley Camberlain wes eleded the\nfirst woman mayar with on all woman council\n1911;\nshe lived in the home as a young,\nsingle women and for a time after her\nmarriage to Thomas Chamberlain, with her\ntwo young sons,\n13. NATHAN ADAMS HOUSE\nThe leg cabin in the back of this properly\nis one of the oldest dwellings in Kanob.\nThe owners lived in the cabin between\n1880 and 1890 while the brick home in\nfront was under construction Musically\ntalented, Nathan was a member of\nKanab\'s first band. He was well known\nas a good cancer\nU.S.89\nTO SALT LAKE,\nBRYCE & ZION\n(89)\n300 North\n200 North\n100 North\nCenter Street\nSENIOR CITIZEN CENTER\n12\n13\n100 South\n200 South\nLEGION HUT\nHOSPITAL\n15\n300 South\n400 South\n2. RIDER/PUGH HOUSE\nIn 18/4 this 1-1/2 story brick Victorian\neclectic pyramid house was built by John\nRider,\na local builder. Rider was a probate\njudge for Kone County from 1889-1996\nThe home has remained in the Rider family.\nSCHOOL\n5. HISTORIC KANAB CITY UBRARY\nBoyd\ndress\nto\nd lay slone while working in Zien\nNational Park building its bridges and\nbuildings. Using stone that was quarned\nJust north o of Kanab, he was the building\nforeman on the library. It is now used as\nThe Kanch Herrage Museum and con be\nvisited during the summer months.\njeans virk\n8. BOWMAN & CO. BUILDING\nBuilt in 1892 by H.E Bowmar, it originally\nhoused a general store. Food samples were\nsold on the main floor, shoes and fabric\nn the basement\nupstairs. The ice fier of ice in the area.\nserved as the only su\nThrough the years, the building was a lumber\nstore, grocery store, hardware store,\nmortuary business and a bank. The old\nfashion safe is still intoc on the main floor.\nToday it is the Rocking V Cafe. While you\nare there ask Victor to show you the sale.\n11. MARIGER-STEWART HOUSE\nBrigham Young was given all of block\ntwenty in the first survey in 1873; it was\nknown as Brigham\'s Block, In 1879 it was\nsold to laurence Moriger. In 1891, the\nhouse was sold to the wife of John Riley\nStewart. Some interesting features are he\nbeautifully kept hand painted wood, made\nto look like oak, the hidden stairs and\nhiding places that were used during the\npolygamy persecution period A turnel was\nbuilt between secret hicing places in the\nhouse to the coal bin by the barn in back.\nCITY PARK\nLIFE\nUTAH\nFLEVATED\n14. LEWIS JEPSON HOME\nThe secone level of this home had one of\nonly wo bath tubs in town. It was used\nas a paptismal font for the townspeople.\nIn 1924, the home was sold to the railroad.\nThe Building was a resting stop for the tourist\nwhere they could enjuy shopping in the\ngift shop located at I front of the building.\nat the f\nPeople who have sloyed here have\nencountered a ghost they call O\'tool. I\'s\nsaid that O\'tool can still be seen and heard\nwalking the halls of the home and restaurant.\nThe Jacobson\'s now own the home and the\nadjacent Jake Chaparrel Restaurant.\nCity of Kanab\nHeritage Walking Tour\nSQUAW TRAIL\nPOOL\nDN\nLIBRARY\n21\nNORTH\n89A\nU.S. 89\nHistoric\nLibrary.\n200 North\n100 North\n3\nABA\nKANABWOOD DR\nMAST\n89\n300 North\n200 South\n3\n3 SIXTUSE JOHNSON\nBuilt in 1891, the onesto y house has a\ngable roof. The foundation is built from\nnalive, red stone which was quarried\nnearby. The actual builder is not known\nSixtus Johnson\'s father, Nephi, is credited\nfor the dacovery of Zior Canyon in 1858.\nSixtus come to Kanab in his youth and was\nemployed by large cattle comparies most\nof his life.\n5\n蓝\n6. KANAB HOTEL\nIn 1929, Guy Chamberlain built the Kanab\nHotel. It was very successful for many years.\nMovie stars such at Clark Gable stayed in\nons of the eleven rooms. Today is the\nhome of Terry Alderman\'s Camera Tracing\nCompany.\nBA\nPHOTO SUPPLIES\n9. MONUMENT TO MAJOR JOHN WESLEY\nPOWELL\nAt this site ir 1870 Major Powell, the first\nman to run the Colorado River, set up tent\nheadquarters and with the aid of a transt,\nestablished the meridian from which surveys\nof the entire area was made.\nVERMILION CIRCLE\n12. JAMES HILL SWAPP HOME\nBuilt in 1890, this pioneer home exemplifies\nthe Mansard syle, typical of mary period\nhomes in Kanab. Well preserved, it gives a\nglympse into the pos. Swapp served as\nsherif from 1896-1910.\nSammmmm\n15. CHARLES R. PUGH HOUS\nThis home was built in 1905 by Robert\nPugh. store for the foundation came\nfrom the home of his father, Edward Pugh.\nEdward built the first rock house, it stood\njust west of this home.\nKANAB\nMODICELLI BOSPOILRO\n16. PARRY LODGE\nThe Farry brothers assisted with the first movies\nmade in Southern Utah, staring Tom Mix in\n\"Deadwood Coach in 1924. They enjoyed\nthe movie business and profited from their\nexperience. In 1931 they opened Parry\nlodge so they could feed and house the\ncast and crews. Stop by and enjoy breakfast\nCEMETERY\n400 South\nNORTH\nU.S.89\nTO LAKE POWELL\nT','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Kanab Heritage Walking Tour\",\n  \"distance\": \"N/A\",\n  \"best_season\": \"N/A\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"N/A\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.0474\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.5263\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"N/A\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"N/A\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Car\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"The trail begins in the city of Kanab, Utah. Visitors can reach Kanab by car via U.S. Highway 89.\",\n  \"description\": \"The Kanab Heritage Walking Tour allows visitors to explore the rich history of the city of Kanab. The tour includes various historic homes and buildings, such as the Heritage House, Johnson/Hicks Hotel and Restaurant, IDS Church and Family History Visitors Center, Stewart & Dilworth Woolley House, Nathan Adams House, Bowman & Co. Building, Mariger-Stewart House, Lewis Jepson Home, Sixtus Johnson House, Kanab Hotel, Monument to Major John Wesley Powell, James Hill Swapp Home, Charles R. Pugh House, and Parry Lodge.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>The Kanab Heritage Walking Tour allows visitors to explore the rich history of the city of Kanab. The tour includes various historic homes and buildings, such as the Heritage House, Johnson/Hicks Hotel and Restaurant, IDS Church and Family History Visitors Center, Stewart & Dilworth Woolley House, Nathan Adams House, Bowman & Co. Building, Mariger-Stewart House, Lewis Jepson Home, Sixtus Johnson House, Kanab Hotel, Monument to Major John Wesley Powell, James Hill Swapp Home, Charles R. Pugh House, and Parry Lodge.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Please respect the privacy of the residents. Some of the homes are not open to the public. The Kanab Heritage Walking Tour can be enjoyed during the summer months. For more information, visit the Kane County Visitors Center located at 78 S 100 E, Kanab, Utah, or call 435.644.5033.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:36','2023-09-22 02:35:52'),(26,'trails',281,'',NULL,'HORSESHOE BEND\nOVERLOOOK HIKE\nOFF THE BEATEN PATE:\nCOLORADO\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nGETTING THERE:\nHORSESHOE BEND\nOVERLOOK HIKE\nHORSESHOE P\nBEND\n72.6 mi\nGLEN CANYON RECREATION AREA\nRIVER\n• From Kanab travel east on HWY 89.\n• Drive 72.6 miles to Page, Arizona.\n• Drive 5 miles and just past milepost 544, watch for the Horseshoe Bend sign on your right.\n.\n• Park in the designated parking area.\n• An entrance fee will be charged per vehicle.\n• Begin your hike at the trailhead.\nMILE\n5\n89\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads ore mpassable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water.\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKonob Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nYEAR ROUND\n1.5 MILES ROUND TRIP\nWALMART\n2.42 mi\nNO\nINDIAN\n2WD\n3 HOURS\nEASY\n4327 FEIT\n1.33 mi\nTINHO\nGLEN\nCANYON\nDAM\nlloneshoe Bend is 5 miles south of\nPage Arizona and is one of the most\nphotographed areas of the Colorado\nRiver. The colors of the rocks chenga\nthroughout the day, the shadows move\nand the river sparkles with varying.\nhues of green and blue. The hike\nis just off the highway and only 1.5\nmiles round hip.It will take you to the op\nof a horseshoe shaped cve look,\nwith the Colorado River 1100 feet below.\nThe trail is acsy to navigate. The overlook\nThe\ncan be dangerous. t is steep so don\'t get\nclose to the cliff edges. In the summer,\nthe uphill hike can be very hot..\nBe sure to bring plenty of water,\nsunscreer and a hat.\nbelow.\n189\nHWY 89 LOOP,\n89\nRESERVATION\nLIFE\nADVENTURE MAP tread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\n98\nPAGE\nKANAB\nMASICALLY UNSPOILE\nFUAVITRIAS\nUT\nAPP\nN\nKANAB\nMICALLY PULSE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Horseshoe Bend Overlook Hike\",\n  \"distance\": \"1.5 miles round trip\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year-round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"4327 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": 36.8796,\n  \"longitude\": -111.5110,\n  \"accessibility\": \"2WD vehicle\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": 3,\n  \"vehicle\": \"2WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, travel east on HWY 89. Drive 72.6 miles to Page, Arizona. Drive 5 miles, and just past milepost 544, watch for the Horseshoe Bend sign on your right. Park in the designated parking area and pay an entrance fee per vehicle. Begin your hike at the trailhead.\",\n  \"description\": \"Horseshoe Bend is 5 miles south of Page, Arizona and is one of the most photographed areas of the Colorado River. The colors of the rocks change throughout the day, the shadows move, and the river sparkles with varying hues of green and blue. The hike is just off the highway and only 1.5 miles round trip. It will take you to the top of a horseshoe-shaped overlook, with the Colorado River 1100 feet below. The trail is easy to navigate.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Horseshoe Bend is 5 miles south of Page, Arizona and is one of the most photographed areas of the Colorado River. The colors of the rocks change throughout the day, the shadows move, and the river sparkles with varying hues of green and blue. The hike is just off the highway and only 1.5 miles round trip. It will take you to the top of a horseshoe-shaped overlook, with the Colorado River 1100 feet below. The trail is easy to navigate.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"<p>Disclaimer: This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Please respect Private Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.</p><p>Kanab Visitor\'s Center: 785 100 E, Phone: 435.644.5033</p>\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:42','2023-09-22 02:36:13'),(27,'trails',282,'',NULL,'HUNTRESS\nSLOT CANYON HIKE\nHUNTRESS\nSLOT CANYON HIKE\nFANAR TRAIL\nUT\nAPP\n106T\n1.3 mi\nADVENTURE MAP\n800\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nDISCLAIMER:\nothers may enjoy.\n2\nGETTING THERE\n• From Karab, drive 11.4 miles north on HWY 89.\nJust post mile post 76 turn right on road 106. and drive for 1.Imie.\n1.1 mi\nYEAR ROUND\n• When the road forks stay left.\nThe road will fork again, stay right. Drive a short distance\n106L\nPark of the turnout, you will hike rood 106T.\n• Hike cown the steep dir hil and head north east in the wash.\n• Hike to the end, there are some awesome water pockets.\n* If you have lime, check out Diana\'s Throne, a popular land mark.\nP\nATV\n5 MILES\n3 HOURS\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the \'rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nNO\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\n106Q\n8173 FEET\nHUNTRESS\nSLOT CANYON\n5\n200\nEASY\nMILE\n4WD REQUIRED\nPAST THIS POINT\ny\nThe Huntress Slot Canyan hike is a colorfu\ncharming conyan with a few toadstool\nmorks. It\'s a twn mila, mourd tip ATV ride\ncr hike in the bottom of a wash slot type\ncanyon. Locals love to trail run in this\ncanyon.\ncanyon. With an ATV, you can get a\nquarter of c mile from the end.\nThe canyon ands in a box canyon\nwith some cool water packet holes. This\nfamily friendly, pet friendly hike, is\nespecially beautiful at sunset. It wil only\nlake a few hours, but you will want la\nkeep exploring. Pictures above is Clara\'s\nThrone, a famous land mark here. You can\n1-4190\nVAS\nhike to Diana\'s throne, there you will sze\nbreathicking views of Zion in the distance.\nThere are many other self guided hikes and\nATV trails in the area to keep you busy.\nGPS 37 11.421\n112 38.734\nCARMEN\nDIANAS\nTHRONE\n284\nLIFE\ntread lightly! TAH\nELEVATED\n11.4 mi KANAB\nMARTENS\nUT\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILE\nKANAB\nMEIL SPEED','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Huntress Slot Canyon Hike\",\n  \"distance\": \"1.3 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year Round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"8173 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.190\",\n  \"longitude\": \"112.38734\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"4WD required\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"Yes\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"3 hours\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"ATV\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 11.4 miles north on Hwy 89. Just past mile post 76, turn right on Road 106 and drive for 1.1 mi. When the road forks, stay left. The road will fork again, stay right. Drive a short distance to the turnout, where you will hike Road 106T. Hike down the steep dirt hill and head northeast in the wash. Hike to the end, where you will find some awesome water pockets. If you have time, check out Diana\'s Throne, a popular landmark.\",\n  \"description\": \"The Huntress Slot Canyon hike is a colorful and charming canyon with a few toadstool marks. It\'s a ten mile, round trip ATV ride or hike in the bottom of a wash slot type canyon. Locals love to trail run in this canyon. With an ATV, you can get a quarter mile from the end. The canyon ends in a box canyon with some cool water pockets. This family-friendly, pet-friendly hike is especially beautiful at sunset. It will only take a few hours, but you will want to keep exploring. You can hike to Diana\'s Throne, where you will see breathtaking views of Zion in the distance. There are many other self-guided hikes and ATV trails in the area to keep you busy.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"The Huntress Slot Canyon hike is a colorful and charming canyon with a few toadstool marks. It\'s a ten mile, round trip ATV ride or hike in the bottom of a wash slot type canyon. Locals love to trail run in this canyon. With an ATV, you can get a quarter mile from the end. The canyon ends in a box canyon with some cool water pockets. This family-friendly, pet-friendly hike is especially beautiful at sunset. It will only take a few hours, but you will want to keep exploring. You can hike to Diana\'s Throne, where you will see breathtaking views of Zion in the distance. There are many other self-guided hikes and ATV trails in the area to keep you busy.\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit.\\n\\nPhone: 435.644.5033\\n\\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\\n\\nLifetime Access: tread lightly!\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:48','2023-09-22 02:36:40'),(28,'trails',283,'',NULL,'380\nJACKSON FLAT RESERVOIR\nSHERRY BELLE TRAIL\nKANAB\nD\n2.82 mi\nCIGOT\n8.9\nKane Plex Drive\n46 mi\nADVENTURE MAP\n單面效益\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\n30 mi\nBIKING:\nHIKING:\nFISHING\nDISK GOLF\nJACKSON FLAT RESERVOIR\nSHERRY BELLE TRAIL\nELEVATION:\nYEAR ROUND\n• Drive a short distance and park here.\n.\nJACKSON\nFLAT\nRESERVOIR\nNO\nGETTING THERE!\n• From Kanab, drive 2.8 miles south on HWY 89A.\n• Turn left on Kaneplex Drive.\n• Make your first left then stay right.\n.\nP\nYES\n5771 FEET\nYES\nYES\nYES\nNOTE:\n.\n• If you are planning on fishing and need a licence. You may purchase one at Claziers Market.\n22 mi\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always chack local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wet. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\"\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nLooking for something different Chees\nout the local watering hole, Jackson Flat\nReservoir! There are endless possibilities of\nfor in the sun. So many fun things to do here:\ndisc golf, fishing, poddle boarding.\nkayoking, and canoeing. The new Shory\nBele Troi is an awesome trail for\nhiking and biking. Its an easy 3.2 mile\nloop around the reservoir with a few lookout\nsours. This trail is pet friendly and dogs musi\nbe on leash. Be sure to use the complimentary\ndoggie bogs when needed. Nothing spoils\nthe view more than unwanted droppings. The\nwild life at the reservoir is impressive; ducks,\ngeese, crows, engles and many other variaty\nof birds. There are frogs, lizards and snakes.\nThe reservair has trout, bass end sun fish\nBring the whole family for loads of fun.\n.50 mi\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nELEVATED\n3.2 mi\nSHERRY\nBELLE\nTRAIL\nFUITES\nAPP\nKANAB\nNORICALLY UNSPOILED\nKANAB\nMY PE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Sherry Belle Trail\",\n  \"distance\": \"2.82 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5771 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": null,\n  \"longitude\": null,\n  \"accessibility\": \"Accessible\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": true,\n  \"reservation_required\": false,\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": null,\n  \"vehicle\": \"Car\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 2.8 miles south on HWY 89A. Turn left on Kaneplex Drive. Make your first left then stay right.\",\n  \"description\": \"Looking for something different? Check out the local watering hole, Jackson Flat Reservoir! There are endless possibilities for fun in the sun. So many fun things to do here: disc golf, fishing, paddleboarding, kayaking, and canoeing. The new Sherry Belle Trail is an awesome trail for hiking and biking. It\'s an easy 3.2-mile loop around the reservoir with a few lookout points. This trail is pet friendly and dogs must be on a leash. Be sure to use the complimentary doggie bags when needed. Nothing spoils the view more than unwanted droppings. The wildlife at the reservoir is impressive; ducks, geese, crows, eagles, and many other varieties of birds. There are frogs, lizards, and snakes. The reservoir has trout, bass, and sunfish. Bring the whole family for loads of fun.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Looking for something different? Check out the local watering hole, Jackson Flat Reservoir! There are endless possibilities for fun in the sun. So many fun things to do here: disc golf, fishing, paddleboarding, kayaking, and canoeing. The new Sherry Belle Trail is an awesome trail for hiking and biking. It\'s an easy 3.2-mile loop around the reservoir with a few lookout points. This trail is pet friendly and dogs must be on a leash. Be sure to use the complimentary doggie bags when needed. Nothing spoils the view more than unwanted droppings. The wildlife at the reservoir is impressive; ducks, geese, crows, eagles, and many other varieties of birds. There are frogs, lizards, and snakes. The reservoir has trout, bass, and sunfish. Bring the whole family for loads of fun.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"If you are planning on fishing and need a license, you may purchase one at Claziers Market. Please respect private property and be prepared for a wilderness experience. Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas. Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy.\",\n}','2023-09-10 06:31:54','2023-09-22 02:37:03'),(29,'trails',284,'',NULL,'JOHNSON CANYON\nDRIVING TOUR\n2.6 mi\n3.1 mi\nOn the left:\n\"The Lion\'s Head\nOn the right\n\"Eagle Gate Arch\n6\n9\n7.5 mi\n3\n4\n3.6 mi On the right: Pioneer grave 5.4 mi\nAgent\n89\nFries\n12\n7.9 mi\nKANAB\nGreat view of the White 5.5 mi\nMountains\nFKD OF\nPAVEMENT\nCHOCODILE HOG CANYON\nTHAILHEAD AND MONIC AREA\n9.5 ml\nJensen.\nSTORE GARAGE\nFRENHIN ARIZONA\nGASELINE LAS\nGE FOR\nJohnson Canyon is a delighful scenic drive that will refresh the soul. You will quickly see why Hollywood used this beautiful\ncanyon as a backdrop for several movies. After turning onto Johnson Canyon Road, stop and reset your car\'s trip meter to\n0.0 miles and enjoy your drive to the fol owing sites. Most points of interest are on private property, but can be easily an oyed\nfrom the road. Bring binoculars to view the Indian and cowboy glyphs. The tour ends where the pavement turns to dirt.\nTurn around and enjoy again the sites of Johnson Canyon.\nHIGHLIGHTS:\n#4- Dairy Canyon, Several important Indian artifacts have beer found in this area and can be seen at the Kanab Heritage\nMuseum in Kanob (260 N 200 W). Call 435 644-3966 for hours.\nLIFE\ntread lightly! UTAH\nFLEVATED\nel\". In years past, this movie sets has been used for numerous Westerns, including several episodes of the\npopular \"Gunsmoke\" TV series.\n13\nOn the right: Pioneer Billboard 9.1 mi\nand Indian Writings\nThese ATV/OHV trailheads are the gateway to some great off-road adventures.\n#14- In 1914 Freddie Crystal rode into Konah with a map that indicated that Montezuma had secreted his treasures to a cave in\nthis canyon. Locals pitched tents and began digging. They discovered multiple chombers, side passages, artifacts and petroglyphs\nbut alas, no gold in those White Cliffs Yet, the legend continues.\nThe Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument. You are now entering the southern boundary of the largest National\nMonument in America. Almos: 2 million acres of bcckcounty advertures: slot canyons, dinosaur fossils, canyoneering, and solitude.\nADVENTURE MAP\n离离\nSKUTUMPAH ROAD\nMILI\n16.2 mi\nOnd\n2017\n5\nNEMA MABINE\nTRACHEAD\nJOHNSON CANYON ROAD\nCATCHLOW\nOn the left: Dairy Canyon 5.4 mi\nSTOP\nSET YOUR\nTRIP METER\nTO ZERO\nN\nCONT\n89\nUT,\nAFP\n10\nOn the left: Crocodile/Hog 7.9 miles on the right: Bunting Ranches 7.9 mi On the right: \"Indian Writings\"\nCanyon trailhead and picnicking\nand \"Cowboy Glyph\nKANAB\nMLY DESPED\nOn the right: \"Old Gunsmoke\nMovie Set\" (1955-1975)\n8\nOn the right: Pioneer farm and 7.0 mi On the right: Sunflowers in the\nsummer fields\nequipment\n14\nBION\nOn the right: Nephi Pasture 11 mi Grand Staircase Escalante, the\n4WD Trailhead\ncanyon to Montezuma\'s Cave\n15\n16\n17\n11.8 mi On the left: Swapp Canyon 11.8 mi On the right: Beautiful sunsets 15.4 mi The right: End of pavement, begin-\nand night skies\nning of backcountry adventure','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Johnson Canyon Driving Tour\",\n  \"distance\": \"2.6 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"\",\n  \"elevation\": \"\",\n  \"latitude\": \"\",\n  \"longitude\": \"\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"Johnson Canyon is a delightful scenic drive that will refresh the soul. You will quickly see why Hollywood used this beautiful canyon as a backdrop for several movies. After turning onto Johnson Canyon Road, stop and reset your car\'s trip meter to 0.0 miles and enjoy your drive to the following sites. Most points of interest are on private property, but can be easily enjoyed from the road. Bring binoculars to view the Indian and cowboy glyphs. The tour ends where the pavement turns to dirt. Turn around and enjoy again the sights of Johnson Canyon.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"- Highlights:\\n\\n#4- Dairy Canyon, Several important Indian artifacts have been found in this area and can be seen at the Kanab Heritage Museum in Kanab (260 N 200 W). Call 435 644-3966 for hours.\\n\\n- These ATV/OHV trailheads are the gateway to some great off-road adventures.\\n\\n#14- In 1914 Freddie Crystal rode into Konah with a map that indicated that Montezuma had secreted his treasures to a cave in this canyon. Locals pitched tents and began digging. They discovered multiple chambers, side passages, artifacts, and petroglyphs but alas, no gold in those White Cliffs. Yet, the legend continues.\\n\\n- The Grand Staircase-Escalante National Monument. You are now entering the southern boundary of the largest National Monument in America. Almost 2 million acres of backcountry adventures: slot canyons, dinosaur fossils, canyoneering, and solitude.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:00','2023-09-22 02:37:20'),(30,'trails',285,'',NULL,'KANAB CREEK\nEXPLORE\nKANAB CREEK\nEXPLORE\nFIECARE MALHEUR\nHOTH\n89\nwww\nRONAL\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nBEST SEASON:\nVEHICLE:\nHIKING:\nAVERAGE TIME:\nDIFFICULTY:\nELEVATION:\nGETTING THERE:\n(P\nBEST FRIENDS\nTURN OFF\nKANAS CREEK AT BEST FRIENDS\nFrom Kancb, drive 5 miles north on HWY 89.\nTurn right after milepost 69.\n2.8 mi\nD\nBEST FRIENDS\nWELCOME!\nCENTER\nSPRING SUMMER FALL\n• From the Best Friends Welcome Center drive 1.4 miles and turn right on the dirt road\n• Drive a short distance and park in the parking area on the right.\n• You can access the creek from here.\nNILE\nKANAB CREEK DAM:\n• As you leave Kanab heading north on HWY 89 drive 1.0 miles.\n9\n• Turn left just on to the dirt road ccross from Hog Canyon.\n. Follow the dirt road to the creek\n• Hike down stream to see the Dam.\nCREEK\nACCESS\nSHORT DISTANCE\nDISCLAIMER:\n\"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and\nweather conditions. Stay on designatec roads. Dirt roads cre mpassable when wel. Please respect\nPrivate Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water\nfood, sunscreen, and suppies Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas!\nDo not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your vist so\nothers may enjoy.\nKanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E\nPHONE: 435.644.5033\nNO\nDAM\nFEW HOURS\n2WD\n5.4 mi\n4970 FEET\nCREEK\nSLOT CANYON\n1.5 mi\nHIDDEN\nLAKE\nEASY\nKANAB\nADVENTURE MAP tread lightly!\n8810\nHOG CANYON\nKarab Crock runs north and south through\nKanb is one of the many tributaries of the\nGrand Canyon. It always has running water.\nA cool little slot canyon near Best Friends\nis a fun spot to explore. The water level\nvares from ankle deep to wast high and\nshould be avoided when it s raining\nor during flood season. Visit Hidden\nLake pictured on the other side of this map.\nYou see where water is seeping from the red\nsandstone and has formed a underground\nlake insice cave. The selfiers used it is cave\nas a cooler, by placing dairy products in a\nboat ied to rope and then pushing the boar\nout in the middle of the cave to stay cool. It is\na 1.5 mile hike from the creek. Dan\'t plan to\nhike up? You will need 4WD from the parking\narea to navigcie the very deep sand.\nGPS 37 8.335\n112 31.996\nLIFE\nUTAH\nCLEVATEO:\nT\nAPP\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILED\n477\nKANAB\nKRYLLY USPOLE','{\n  \"trail_name\": \"Kanab Creek\",\n  \"distance\": \"2.8 mi\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Spring, Summer, Fall\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Easy\",\n  \"elevation\": \"4970 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.139\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.533\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"2WD\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Few hours\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"2WD\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"From Kanab, drive 5 miles north on HWY 89. Turn right after milepost 69.\",\n  \"description\": \"Kanab Creek runs north and south through Kanab and is one of the many tributaries of the Grand Canyon. It always has running water. A cool little slot canyon near Best Friends is a fun spot to explore. The water level varies from ankle deep to waist high and should be avoided when it\'s raining or during flood season. Visit Hidden Lake, pictured on the other side of this map, where water is seeping from the red sandstone and has formed an underground lake inside a cave. The locals used this cave as a cooler by placing dairy products in a boat tied to a rope and then pushing the boat out in the middle of the cave to stay cool. It is a 1.5 mile hike from the creek. Don\'t plan to hike up? You will need 4WD from the parking area to navigate the very deep sand.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Kanab Creek runs north and south through Kanab and is one of the many tributaries of the Grand Canyon. It always has running water. A cool little slot canyon near Best Friends is a fun spot to explore. The water level varies from ankle deep to waist high and should be avoided when it\'s raining or during flood season. Visit Hidden Lake, pictured on the other side of this map, where water is seeping from the red sandstone and has formed an underground lake inside a cave. The locals used this cave as a cooler by placing dairy products in a boat tied to a rope and then pushing the boat out in the middle of the cave to stay cool. It is a 1.5 mile hike from the creek. Don\'t plan to hike up? You will need 4WD from the parking area to navigate the very deep sand.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads may be impassable when wet. Please respect private property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas! Do not remove artifacts or deface the rock art. Leave no trace of your visit so others may enjoy. Kanab Visitor\'s Center: 78 5 100 E, PHONE: 435.644.5033\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:08','2023-09-22 02:37:43'),(31,'trails',286,'',NULL,'SOUTHERN UTAHA\nAREA MAP\nKANAB\nMAGICALLY UNSPOILED\nCheck locally for road\nand weather conditions.\nDo not drive on dirt\nroads when wet.\nUTAH ROAD\nCONDITIONS:\n800.492.2400\nLIFE\nLITAH\nELEVATED\n+\nST. GEORGE\nHum\nCedar\nCly\nDuck Creek Village\nGrand Canyon\nGrand Staircase\nHorseshoe Bend\nLake Powell\nMt.Carmel Junction\nPipe Spring\nZion\nAIRPORTS\nLas Vegas\nSalt Lake City\nSt. George\nPhoenix\nKoko\nApple\nviiley\nMILEAGE FROM KANAB\nAntelope Canyon\nBryce Canyon\nCoral Pink Sand Dunes\nSpringd\nREFERENS\nw▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬www.\n76\n77\n77\n23\n55\n78\n15\n73\n17\nZICH\nNATIONAL\nPARK\n21\n40\n350\nkkk\n200\n317\n8