 your left. The trail starts behind the information sign on Road 100. Continue on Road 100 for 3.9 miles to the Hog Canyon turn-off and turn left on Road 104. Continue on Road 104 for another 7.9 miles. The trail starts behind the Mansard sign.\",\n  \"description\": \"The Mansard ATV Trail is a challenging off-road adventure in Hog Canyon. It offers stunning views, unique petroglyphs, and a thrilling experience for ATV enthusiasts. The trail is 7.9 miles long and is best enjoyed year-round, although weather conditions may affect accessibility. The last 2 miles of the trail are particularly challenging, with rocky terrain and steep climbs.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>The Mansard ATV Trail is a challenging off-road adventure in Hog Canyon. It offers stunning views, unique petroglyphs, and a thrilling experience for ATV enthusiasts. The trail is 7.9 miles long and is best enjoyed year-round, although weather conditions may affect accessibility. The last 2 miles of the trail are particularly challenging, with rocky terrain and steep climbs.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": {\n    \"address\": \"785 100 E, Kanab, UT\",\n    \"phone\": \"435-644-5033\",\n    \"parking\": \"Available\",\n    \"petroglyphs\": true,\n    \"tread_lightly\": true,\n    \"advisories\": [\n      \"The trail is for ATV use only\",\n      \"The last 2 miles are challenging\",\n      \"Respect the petroglyphs and do not touch or walk on them\"\n    ]\n  }\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:40','2023-09-22 02:39:23'),(37,'trails',292,'',NULL,'MANSARD\nFILE\nMANSARD\nBIKE\nCanyon\nRMILION\n26441\nFOTO\nKANAB 6.5 IN\n20\nWA\n5940T\nEAST\n894RT\nOFF THE BEATEN PATH:\nPERMITTING\nThishika Inyol airmacusó relle round trip\nHilamcending more than 1000 let na\nsundalone alcove filled with andeat petroglyphs.\nBEST SEASON: YEAR ROUND WEATHER Along the trail you will enjoy many beautiful\nrock formations and spectacular views of the\nYaron Chifa, Kalbab Plateau and al\nKanals. You will be hiking aloep men\nenrain and