"6.5 miles round trip\",\n  \"best_season\": \"Year round\",\n  \"difficulty\": \"Steep and strenuous\",\n  \"elevation\": \"5940 feet\",\n  \"latitude\": \"37.048134\",\n  \"longitude\": \"-112.430899\",\n  \"accessibility\": \"Any vehicle\",\n  \"pets_allowed\": \"No\",\n  \"reservation_required\": \"No\",\n  \"average_hours_to_hike\": \"Half day\",\n  \"vehicle\": \"Any\",\n  \"getting_there\": \"Drive 6.5 miles east of Kanab just past milepost 59 and turn left on onto Vista Drive Road. Turn right on Grand Vermilion Avenue. Turn left on Coyote Canyon. Turn left on Rocky Ledge Lane. Go through the gate onto road #1051. Stay right at the Y in the road on #1054. The left goes to the water tank. When the road ends, park here. The trail will begin here.\",\n  \"description\": \"Thishika Inyol airstrip round trip, hiking more than 1000 feet in elevation to a secluded alcove filled with ancient petroglyphs. Along the trail, you will enjoy many beautiful rock formations and spectacular views of the Yaron Chifa, Kanab Plateau, and al Kanals. The hike is steep and strenuous, with some scrambling required to negotiate a seven-foot sandstone ledge and the sandy hill to the top. The Monacid alcove is unique and features deeply grooved sides dating back to the Aasta period (0 AD to 1250 AD). It is uncommon to see rock art on the floor of a remarkable place, so please don\'t touch or walk on the petroglyphs. Respect and protect this special area.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Thishika Inyol airstrip round trip, hiking more than 1000 feet in elevation to a secluded alcove filled with ancient petroglyphs. Along the trail, you will enjoy many beautiful rock formations and spectacular views of the Yaron Chifa, Kanab Plateau, and al Kanals. The hike is steep and strenuous, with some scrambling required to negotiate a seven-foot sandstone ledge and the sandy hill to the top. The Monacid alcove is unique and features deeply grooved sides dating back to the Aasta period (0 AD to 1250 AD). It is uncommon to see rock art on the floor of a remarkable place, so please don\'t touch or walk on the petroglyphs. Respect and protect this special area.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": \"Be prepared for hiking in hot weather. Be sure to bring plenty of water.\\nDisclaimer: This map and directions are intended for general reference only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads are impassable when wet. Respect private property. Prepare for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra water, food, sunscreen, and supplies. Cell phone service is non-existent in most areas. Leave no trace of your visit so that others may enjoy.\"\n}','2023-09-10 06:32:46','2023-09-22 02:39:49'),(38,'trails',293,'',NULL,'MOUNTAIN BIKING\nBASECAMP KANAB, UTAH\nRAVEN/ROADRUNNER TRAIL\n2 mi loop with more to come\n100 ft climb\neasy to moderate\nHOG CANYON (fat bike trail)\n8.6 mi out and back\n900 ft climb\nmoderate\nI GOOSEBERRY MESA SLICKROCK\n11.9 mi loop\n900 ft gain\nmoderate\nNAVAJO LAKE/VIRGIN RIVER TRAIL\n11.4 mi\n1020 ft gain\nmoderate\nPAGE RIM TRAIL\n10.3 mi loop\n652 ft gain\nall skill levels.\nGOOSEBERRY MESA WINDMILL TRAIL THUNDER MOUNTAIN\n5.3 mi figure 8 loop\n174 ft gain\ndifficult in spots\nPANORAMA TRAIL\n6 mi loop\n370 ft gain\nall skill levels\nGOOSEBERRY MESA\nWINDMILL LOOP\n-113 9.973, 37 9.09\nMOUNTAIN BIKING\nBASECAMP KANAB, UTAH\nVIRGIN RIVER RIM TRAIL\n-112 55.032, 37 35.455\nCASTO CANYON TRAIL\n-112 17.062, 37 48.174\nNAVAJO LAKE LOOP TRAIL\n-112 49.303, 37 32.02\nWASHINGTON CO.\nEPIC VIRGIN RIVER RIM TRAIL\n-112 42.129, 37 26.284\nBasecamp Kanab, UTAH is the perfect basecamp for your mountain biking adventures. It\'s centrally ocated in the\nmiddle of three National Parks: Zion, Bryce, the Grand Canyon and Lake Powell. Ride a new trail each day then lodge\nand dine in Kanab. You will find great lodging options FROM budget and luxury hotels, camping and RV sites. Within\nan hour, you can choose over a dozen spe