": [\n    \"Start at the center of town and head north on 100 East.\",\n    \"When you get to the bend in the road by Farry Lodge, stay right on 100 East.\",\n    \"Behind the ball fields you will see the trailhead for the Squaw Trail.\",\n    \"Follow Squaw trail until you see the sign on your right for the Roadrunner trail.\",\n    \"There is additional parking if you head west along the back of the ball fields and on the other side of the dike.\"\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Raven/Roadrunner is a short mountain bike challenge in the heart of Kanab, but you may choose to hike it. This is the first completed section of an extensive planned mountain bike trail system. It is best to do this trail clockwise. Intermediate and experienced level mountain bikers will enjoy these trails winding through red rock and beautiful landscapes. This would also be a fun trail for a family hike. Bikers and hikers will find the trailhead just west of Squaw Trail north of Kanab City\'s Jacob Hamblin Park. There are many hikes that start from the Squaw Trail.\",\n  \"description_html\": \"<p>Raven/Roadrunner is a short mountain bike challenge in the heart of Kanab, but you may choose to hike it. This is the first completed section of an extensive planned mountain bike trail system. It is best to do this trail clockwise. Intermediate and experienced level mountain bikers will enjoy these trails winding through red rock and beautiful landscapes. This would also be a fun trail for a family hike. Bikers and hikers will find the trailhead just west of Squaw Trail north of Kanab City\'s Jacob Hamblin Park. There are many hikes that start from the Squaw Trail.</p>\",\n  \"additional_info\": {\n    \"disclaimer\": \"This map and directions are intended for general reference use only. Always check local road and weather conditions. Stay on designated roads. Dirt roads can become impassable when wet. Please respect Private Property. Be prepared for a wilderness experience: Always bring extra wate